IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sga2-nouns`
IMPORT `sga2-s76a-consequences`

-- Tests for sga2-s76a-consequences.l4: s 76A(1) to (15) of the Companies Act 1967 (Singapore).
-- Expected values are written from the text (inputs/CoA1967.txt lines 8092-8311), beside each assertion, before the code was run.
-- Where the text does not say no in its own words, the answer is NOTHING; JUST FALSE appears only where it does (the Guide's ruling of 2026-10-29).


§ `s 76A(1): void contracts and transactions`

-- Arguments: the kind of contract or transaction; made or entered into in contravention of section 76.
#ASSERT `s 76A(1) the contract or transaction is void` `s 76A(1)(a) a contract or transaction by which a company acquires or purports to acquire its own shares or units of its own shares, or shares or units of shares in its holding company or ultimate holding company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(1) the contract or transaction is void` `s 76A(1)(b) a contract or transaction by which a company lends money on the security of its own shares or units of its own shares, or of shares or units of shares in its holding company or ultimate holding company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not made in contravention of section 76: the subsection avoids only those that were; it says nothing of these.
#ASSERT `s 76A(1) the contract or transaction is void` `s 76A(1)(a) a contract or transaction by which a company acquires or purports to acquire its own shares or units of its own shares, or shares or units of shares in its holding company or ultimate holding company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(1) the contract or transaction is void` `s 76A(1)(b) a contract or transaction by which a company lends money on the security of its own shares or units of its own shares, or of shares or units of shares in its holding company or ultimate holding company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A kind not listed: the list is not closed with "only".
#ASSERT `s 76A(1) the contract or transaction is void` `s 76A(1) some other contract or transaction` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 76A(1A): book-entry securities`

-- "Subsection (1) does not apply to a disposition of book-entry securities": a flat negative.
#ASSERT `s 76A(1A) subsection (1) applies to the disposition` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(1A) subsection (1) applies to the disposition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Court's power to order a transfer: where the Court is satisfied, on the application of the Registrar or any other person (group G1).
-- Arguments: a disposition of book-entry securities; the Court is satisfied that it would be void; an application has been made.
#ASSERT `s 76A(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 76A(2): voidable at the option of the company`

-- Arguments: made in contravention; related to one made in contravention; void under (1); subsection (6) protects.
-- Made in contravention, not void under (1), not protected: voidable.
#ASSERT `s 76A(2) the contract or transaction is one to which subsection (2) applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "or a contract or transaction related to such contract or transaction": a related one is voidable too.
#ASSERT `s 76A(2) the contract or transaction is one to which subsection (2) applies` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to subsection (1)": a void contract is dealt with by (1); (2) says nothing of its being also voidable.
#ASSERT `s 76A(2) the contract or transaction is one to which subsection (2) applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (6)(b): a contract made in reliance on a certificate "is not voidable under subsection (2)": a flat negative.
#ASSERT `s 76A(2) the contract or transaction is one to which subsection (2) applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither made in contravention nor related to one: the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 76A(2) the contract or transaction is one to which subsection (2) applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The company's avoiding: written notice to the other party or parties, where subsection (2) applies.
#ASSERT `s 76A(2) the company may avoid the contract or transaction by written notice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(2) the company may avoid the contract or transaction by written notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(2) the company may avoid the contract or transaction by written notice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 76A(3): who the Court may authorise`

#ASSERT `s 76A(3) the Court may authorise the applicant to give notice in the name of the company` `s 76A(3) a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(3) the Court may authorise the applicant to give notice in the name of the company` `s 76A(3) a holder of debentures of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(3) the Court may authorise the applicant to give notice in the name of the company` `s 76A(3) a trustee for the holders of debentures of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(3) the Court may authorise the applicant to give notice in the name of the company` `s 76A(3) a director of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A grant to a named complement: the text says nothing of anyone else (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1).
#ASSERT `s 76A(3) the Court may authorise the applicant to give notice in the name of the company` `s 76A(3) some other person` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 76A(4): the Court's orders against a person`

-- Arguments: a company makes or performs a contract; in contravention of section 76 or related; the Court is satisfied of loss or damage; a party; the company; one who aided, abetted, counselled or procured.
#ASSERT `s 76A(4) the Court may make an order against the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(4) the Court may make an order against the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(4) the Court may make an order against the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a party, not the company, and no part in the contravention: no order against that person (a "may" gated by "where": group G1).
#ASSERT `s 76A(4) the Court may make an order against the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(4) the Court may make an order against the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(4) the Court may make an order against the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(4) the Court may make an order against the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 76A(5): the orders mentioned`

#ASSERT `s 76A(5) the order is one of the orders mentioned in subsection (5)` `s 76A(5)(a) an order directing a person to refund money or return property to the company or to another person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(5) the order is one of the orders mentioned in subsection (5)` `s 76A(5)(b) an order directing a person to pay to the company or to another person a specified amount of the loss or damage suffered` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(5) the order is one of the orders mentioned in subsection (5)` `s 76A(5)(c) an order directing a person to indemnify the company or another person against loss or damage that may be suffered as a result of the contract or transaction or of its being or having become void` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "include": the list is open; another order is for (4)'s own "just and equitable".
#ASSERT `s 76A(5) the order is one of the orders mentioned in subsection (5)` `s 76A(5) some other order` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 76A(6): the certificate`

-- Arguments: number of directors who signed; a director and a secretary signed; states the requirements were complied with; given to the person.
#ASSERT `s 76A(6) the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` 2 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(6) the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(6) the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One director alone is not enough.
#ASSERT `s 76A(6) the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` 1 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(6) the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(6) the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` 2 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(6) the certificate is one that subsection (6) speaks of` 2 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6)(a): arguments: a certificate subsection (6) speaks of; in reliance on it; the Court has declared under (7) that (6) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 76A(6)(a) the person is under a liability to have an order made against the person under subsection (4)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(6)(a) the person is under a liability to have an order made against the person under subsection (4)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(6)(a) the person is under a liability to have an order made against the person under subsection (4)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Once the Court has made the declaration under (7), (6) does not apply and says nothing; (4) decides.
#ASSERT `s 76A(6)(a) the person is under a liability to have an order made against the person under subsection (4)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6)(b): "is not invalid, and is not voidable under subsection (2)".
#ASSERT `s 76A(6)(b) the contract or transaction is invalid or voidable under subsection (2) by reason of the contravention` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(6)(b) the contract or transaction is invalid or voidable under subsection (2) by reason of the contravention` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(6)(b) the contract or transaction is invalid or voidable under subsection (2) by reason of the contravention` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 76A(7): the Court's declaration that (6) does not apply`

-- Arguments: the application was made by the company or by a person who has suffered loss or damage; the Court has declared that it is satisfied the person became aware before the contract was made.
#ASSERT `s 76A(7) subsection (6) does not apply to the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(7) subsection (6) does not apply to the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(7) subsection (6) does not apply to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 76A(8) to (10): presumptions`

-- (8): arguments: an employee or agent was aware of the matter; proof to the contrary.
#ASSERT `s 76A(8) the person is deemed to have been aware of the matter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(8) the person is deemed to have been aware of the matter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No employee or agent was aware: the deeming says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 76A(8) the person is deemed to have been aware of the matter` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9): arguments: the document purports to be a certificate given under (6); proof to the contrary.
#ASSERT `s 76A(9) the document is deemed to be a certificate given under subsection (6) and duly given` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(9) the document is deemed to be a certificate given under subsection (6) and duly given` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(9) the document is deemed to be a certificate given under subsection (6) and duly given` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (10): arguments: the person has possession of a certificate; proof to the contrary.
#ASSERT `s 76A(10) the person is deemed to be the person to whom the certificate was given` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(10) the person is deemed to be the person to whom the certificate was given` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(10) the person is deemed to be the person to whom the certificate was given` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 76A(11) and (12): signing a false certificate`

-- Arguments: the person signed a certificate; any of the requirements had not been complied with at the time.
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both".
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 76 penalty` OF 5000, 12, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 76A(11) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 76 penalty` OF 5000, 12, TRUE))
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (12): "a defence ... if the defendant proves that ... he or she believed on reasonable grounds".
#ASSERT `s 76A(12) the subsection gives the defendant a defence on these facts` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(12) the subsection gives the defendant a defence on these facts` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Guilty under (11) and no defence is made out: guilty; with the defence made out: not guilty (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence and subsection (12) gives no defence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence and subsection (12) gives no defence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence and subsection (12) gives no defence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(11) the person is guilty of the offence and subsection (12) gives no defence` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The prohibition on signing a certificate that the requirements have been complied with when any had not: BREACH by the act, RESIDUAL without it.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 76A(11) a person must not sign a certificate that the requirements have been complied with when any had not` "Lim Wei Ling" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Individual "Lim Wei Ling") DOES `s 76A(11) sign a certificate that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) have been complied with, when any of them had not` AT 4

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 76A(11) a person must not sign a certificate that the requirements have been complied with when any had not` "Lim Wei Ling" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 9)

§ `s 76A(13) to (15): relief, related contracts, other rights`

#ASSERT `s 76A(13) the power of the Court under section 391 extends to relieving the person from the liability to have an order made under subsection (4)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(13) the power of the Court under section 391 extends to relieving the person from the liability to have an order made under subsection (4)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (14): arguments: the company makes a contract or engages in a transaction under which it gives assistance under s 76(1) or lends under s 76(1A)(b); the other contract is made as a result of or in relation to that assistance or money.
#ASSERT `s 76A(14) the other contract or transaction is deemed to be related to the firstmentioned one` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A deeming adds to the ordinary meaning of "related"; it does not say that another contract is not related.
#ASSERT `s 76A(14) the other contract or transaction is deemed to be related to the firstmentioned one` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(14) the other contract or transaction is deemed to be related to the firstmentioned one` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(15) the right or liability is in addition to the rights and liabilities of the person apart from the section` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(15) the right or liability is in addition to the rights and liabilities of the person apart from the section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: arises under the section or under its order; inconsistent with a right or liability apart from the section.
#ASSERT `s 76A(15) the section or the order prevails over the inconsistent right or liability` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76A(15) the section or the order prevails over the inconsistent right or liability` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76A(15) the section or the order prevails over the inconsistent right or liability` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
